<div class="docs-article">
  <h1>4. Client-Side SPA Router (driftjs-router)</h1>
  <p class="lead-text">
    <code>driftjs-router</code> provides single-page application navigation with history, hash, and memory drivers, dynamic route parameters, nested routes/outlets, and navigation guards.
  </p>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <h2>Initializing the Router</h2>
  <div class="code-block">
    <pre><code>import &#123; createRouter, createWebHistory, createWebHashHistory &#125; from 'driftjs-router';
import HomeView from './views/HomeView.drift';
import UserDetailView from './views/UserDetailView.drift';

export const router = createRouter(&#123;
  history: createWebHistory(),
  routes: [
    &#123; path: '/', component: HomeView &#125;,
    &#123; path: '/users/:id', component: UserDetailView &#125;,
  ],
&#125;);</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2>Providing Router Context in App.drift</h2>
  <p>Provide the router instance using DriftJS native Context API:</p>
  <div class="code-block">
    <pre><code>&lt;script&gt;
  import &#123; RouterContext, RouterView, RouterLink &#125; from 'driftjs-router';
  import &#123; router &#125; from './routes';

  RouterContext.provide(router);
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;nav&gt;
  &lt;RouterLink to="/" label="Home" /&gt;
  &lt;RouterLink to="/users/ada" label="Ada's Profile" /&gt;
&lt;/nav&gt;

&lt;main&gt;
  &lt;RouterView /&gt;
&lt;/main&gt;</code></pre>
  </div>

  <h2>Navigation Guards</h2>
  <p>Protect routes and handle redirects with global and route-level guards:</p>
  <div class="code-block">
    <pre><code>router.beforeEach((to, from) =&gt; &#123;
  if (to.path.startsWith('/admin') &amp;&amp; !isAuthenticated()) &#123;
    return '/login';
  &#125;
  return true;
&#125;);</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>
